28. My practical recommendation

Do not create 130 tables now.

Use this sequence:

Wave 1: 10 core runtime tables
Wave 2: 12 productivity/layout tables
Wave 3: dashboard/widget/grid/form runtime
Wave 4: branding/i18n/help/tours
Wave 5: publishing/versioning/audit
Wave 6: feature flags/search/notifications
Wave 7: AI workspace context
Wave 8: WebOS session/window behavior
Wave 9: telemetry/analytics
Wave 10: full UI Manager Studio

Best immediate enterprise build:

10 core tables
+ 7 productivity tables
+ UI-OS Manager API
+ Angular renderers
+ admin dashboard builder later

Final verdict: the full enterprise UI-OS can be 100+ tables and 20+ backend managers, but Shahin should start with 17 tables and the manager/renderer architecture.